# The HTTP form of a proto contract: the HTTP variation point attached to a
# service that already has the gRPC one, serving the same contract over HTTP.
# Besides the HTTP form, the example adds AddItem and ListItems over lists kept
# by the process while it runs (KeptLists of Todo.Application, which refuses a
# title a list holds): the HTTP variation point adds a way to call
# the application, not a store. They show a path parameter, 201, 404, 409, and
# a deprecated method; those commands are why the gRPC endpoint, its scenarios,
# the module's project, and its registration (TodoModule.cs) change.
base library/architecture/dotnet/vp-grpc-api-in-dotnet.skill/examples
examples examples-proto
change src/App/App.Host/Program.cs
change src/App/App.Host/App.Host.csproj
change Directory.Packages.props
change Todo.slnx
change Makefile
change README.md
change .gitignore
change docs/integration/api/todo/todo.proto
change src/App/App.Host/Api/Grpc/Endpoint/ItemsHandler.cs
change src/App/App.Host.Tests/features/Grpc/items.feature
change src/App/App.Host.Tests/Steps/Grpc/ItemsServiceSteps.cs
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application/Todo.Application.csproj
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application/TodoModule.cs
change src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Domain/Errors/TodoErrors.cs
# The handlers' scenarios sit in Commands/ (features/ and Steps/ per folder of
# the project they test); until its base takes the same layout, the old place
# of the scenario of PlanItems is moved, not edited.
delete src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application.Tests/Steps/PlanItemsSteps.cs
delete src/Modules/Todo/Todo.Application.Tests/features/plan-items.feature
